"[\n    {\n        \"type\": \"title\",\n        \"content\": \"Key Financial & Operational Risks for Sonoco Products Co.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"paragraph\",\n        \"content\": \"The 2025\u20112026 reporting period reflects a massive transformation driven by the $3.8\u202fbn Eviosys acquisition and the divestiture of the Thermoformed & Flexibles Packaging business. While sales, EBITDA and net income have surged, the balance sheet now carries $4.3\u202fbn of debt, significant integration work, and a suite of contingent liabilities that could strain liquidity and dilute shareholders.\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"bullets\",\n        \"content\": [\n            \"\u2022 Integration risk: $1.4\u202fbn of goodwill tied to Eviosys; no impairments recorded yet, but any under\u2011performance could trigger a large write\u2011down.\",\n            \"\u2022 Debt profile: $1.78\u202fbn senior unsecured notes (issued to fund Eviosys) + $700\u202fm term\u2011loan (maturing Dec\u202f2026) + $1.37\u202fbn of debt maturing within 12\u202fmonths. Heavy reliance on a $1.25\u202fbn revolving facility and modest operating cash flow ($0.69\u202fbn) creates refinancing and covenant\u2011compliance pressure, especially with floating\u2011rate exposure.\",\n            \"\u2022 Liquidity cushion is thin: cash & cash equivalents $378\u202fm (plus $193\u202fm foreign\u2011held) versus total debt, current ratio ~1.0, and a large portion of cash tied up overseas, limiting immediate access in a market\u2011stress scenario.\",\n            \"\u2022 Contingent consideration: Up to $725\u202fm linked to the pending ThermoSafe divestiture could materialize as additional cash outflow or debt, eroding the liquidity gains from the sale.\",\n            \"\u2022 Foreign\u2011currency risk: Significant exposure to EUR, GBP, PLN and emerging\u2011market currencies; recent periods benefited from a $454\u202fm translation gain, but a reversal would hit earnings and cash flow.\",\n            \"\u2022 Equity dilution vector: PCSU awards (31,196 units) and RSU/SSAR balances can vest only if 2026\u20112028 performance targets are met, potentially adding share count and diluting earnings if targets are exceeded.\",\n            \"\u2022 Governance red flags: Recent board turnover (loss of seasoned independents) and disclosed family relationships between CEO and chairman could weaken oversight; the unsecured Rabbi\u2011trust holding $4.9\u202fm of deferred compensation is vulnerable in a bankruptcy scenario.\",\n            \"\u2022 Executive compensation anomaly: $3\u202fm cash bonus paid to former President for the ThermoSafe divestiture is unusually large compared to standard severance, suggesting possible precedents for discretionary payouts.\",\n            \"\u2022 ESG & environmental liabilities: While current environmental liabilities are modest ($1.7\u202fm), the company\u2019s sustainability strategy and regulatory scrutiny could raise future compliance costs.\",\n            \"\u2022 Succession uncertainty: 8\u2011K amendment deferring COO retirement indicates potential instability in senior management succession planning.\"\n        ]\n    }\n]"